# vtcon-amiga -- vtcon for a window in the AMIGA personality.
#
# console.device fills the area a clear or scroll leaves with the window's
# one background, never with the colour the program has set (the engine's
# blank_cell in the AMIGA personality). vtcon declares bce (back colour
# erase); a program told bce skips the repaint of its background after a
# clear and so leaves the old background where console.device put it. This
# entry is vtcon without bce, so TERM describes the window.
#
# console.device also wraps at once: the character in the last column puts
# the cursor on the next row (at the bottom right the window scrolls), where
# vtcon (xterm) holds it in the last column until the next character (xenl).
# A program told xenl writes a full row and then CR LF, and on this window
# that moves two rows: every second row is skipped (W-N1, measured on the ROM
# console in the conformance matrix, engine: the AMIGA branch of the printable
# run in engine/vtengine.c). So no xenl either. vsh gets it for
# AMIGA windows from the console (ACTION_VTCON_ENV, handler/slash.c).
#
# Build after terminfo/vtcon.terminfo: tic -x -o <dir> terminfo/vtcon-amiga.terminfo
vtcon-amiga|vtcon Amiga console (AMIGA personality, no back colour erase, wraps at once),
	bce@, xenl@, use=vtcon,
